  faqs: [
    { question: "Is there an IB or IGCSE school in Asansol?", answer: "Not one that's confirmed, no, and that holds for Durgapur next door too. St. Patrick's Higher Secondary School and St. Vincent's High and Technical School stick to ICSE, and the bulk of Asansol's schools sit under the West Bengal Board of Secondary Education instead. The closest schools actually teaching IB or IGCSE are out in Kolkata, a good four hours away, which is exactly why online tutoring carries so much of the weight here." },
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor for my child in Asansol?", answer: "Tell IB Gram the programme, subject, level and exam sitting your child is working toward, and a shortlist comes back of people who have actually taught that syllabus before. Location barely factors in, given there's no Asansol school running the IB to begin with; fit against the syllabus is what drives it. A free trial happens online first, and if it doesn't click, another tutor gets suggested." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE tutors in Asansol for Cambridge and Edexcel?", answer: "Both boards, yes, and always as online tuition rather than a visit to your home. On the Cambridge side, matching runs off the actual code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended, say, or Chemistry 0620; Edexcel students get matched by specification and Foundation or Higher tier instead, working from that board's own papers and mark schemes throughout." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Asansol?", answer: "They don't, no. That kind of doorstep tuition exists only around Gurugram and pockets of Delhi NCR; an Asansol lesson, like almost everywhere else in the country, happens live over video with a shared screen, one to one. It's genuine private tuition delivered to your home online, just not a tutor physically walking through the door." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor cost for a family in Asansol?", answer: "It moves with the programme and level, the subject itself, how long each session runs, and how recently a tutor has actually taught that course, and the number gets confirmed in writing before your trial, not after. HL Diploma subjects tend to cost more than MYP or Core IGCSE work. Nothing gets added for travel since every lesson is online, and no contract locks you in past that." },
    { question: "Which schools near Asansol offer IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None within Asansol or Durgapur itself. Kolkata is where the confirmed options sit: RP Goenka International School in Alipore covers the IB PYP, Cambridge Lower Secondary and IGCSE, and then the IB Diploma, while Calcutta International School in Anandapur runs IB alongside A Level. Both are roughly a four-hour trip from Asansol." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I have to commit?", answer: "There is, on every match. Your child sits through an actual lesson from their real syllabus with the tutor online, no fee attached and no obligation to book anything further. A short plan for the first month follows the trial, and from there it's your call: go ahead, ask for tweaks, or try a different tutor altogether." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for an Asansol student?", answer: "Guidance, yes; writing it for them, never. That means helping shape a workable research question, unpacking what each criterion is actually looking for, thinking through data collection, and giving blunt feedback on a draft. The line stops the moment a tutor would be putting words or working directly into the graded document itself, since that crosses into an integrity breach IB Gram won't touch." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with in Asansol?", answer: "Coverage runs across the core Diploma groups, and the ones Asansol families ask for most are Maths Analysis and Approaches, Applications and Interpretation, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay support alongside them." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students in Asansol, not just the Diploma?", answer: "The whole continuum is covered, not only the Diploma end. MYP sessions for Asansol students usually centre on criterion-level writing in the sciences and in Language and Literature, plus building out the Personal Project's journal. PYP work covers early reading, writing and number confidence along with Exhibition research skills, typically in shorter, frequent sessions that also help a recently transferred child settle back into a routine." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for an Asansol student?", answer: "Here it's arguably the better option rather than a compromise, simply because no Asansol school teaches IB or IGCSE for it to compete against. A shared screen, marked past papers and recorded worked examples cover almost everything a classroom session would, and it opens the door to specialists from across the country instead of whoever happens to live nearby." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Asansol students?", answer: "Before ever being introduced to a family, a tutor's qualifications, recent teaching history with that specific subject and level, and their grasp of the actual assessment criteria all get checked. With no local school to benchmark against, the bar is recent, relevant teaching experience rather than a general qualification. Everything else gets confirmed by you directly in the trial lesson." },
    { question: "When should my child in Asansol start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Right at the start of the course works best, Class 11 for the Diploma, Grade 9 for IGCSE, so there's room to fix weak spots before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all start landing. Starting later, even in the final year, still moves the needle if sessions focus tightly on the highest-value topics and past-paper practice." },
    { question: "My child is switching from WBBSE or ICSE to IB or IGCSE in Asansol. Can a tutor help?", answer: "This comes up often, mostly because there's no local school offering a gentle, in-school route between boards. Content usually isn't the real problem; it's the question style, learning to actually explain, evaluate and justify rather than recall, plus getting comfortable with IA or coursework planning early, ideally starting the summer before the switch happens." },
    { question: "Can sessions run on weekends or after school hours in Asansol?", answer: "They can, and most families do exactly that, weekday evenings after school plus weekend mornings. The schedule also bends around Asansol's brutal pre-monsoon heat and the Durga Puja, Kali Puja and Chhath Puja breaks. Since everything runs online, squeezing in a second weekly session before mocks is straightforward." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor assigned in Asansol?", answer: "Say so, and a different tutor gets found. Check-ins happen with families every few weeks specifically to catch this early, and a swap is offered whenever something isn't working rather than expecting a child to push through it. No contract ties you down, so pausing or stopping altogether is always an option too." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school in Asansol or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "It isn't. IB Gram runs as an independent tutoring service with no tie, endorsement or representation from any school in Asansol, Kolkata or elsewhere, nor from the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Schools get named here only to describe the region's real curriculum options, and tutors work strictly to each school's calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

